### Pull requests

- My GitHub (personal + pickforge accounts) runs an automated **Codex PR review** (`chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]`).
- It reviews **once**, automatically, when a PR is **opened**. It does **not** re-review later pushes, and `@codex review` comments do **nothing** — don't post them, don't poll for a second review.
- After opening a PR, **wait** for that single review to land (poll the PR's reviews/inline comments — a few minutes), then triage. Fix the **valid, correct** findings (not false positives); briefly say why any finding is dismissed.
- Because there's no re-review, batch work so the important code is present when the PR is first opened. If a later batch genuinely needs a Codex pass, that means **opening a fresh PR** (open is the only trigger).
- Don't merge a PR until its (one) Codex review has been addressed.

